- main:
  - heading "The official home of RFCs" [level=1]
  - link "What is an RFC?":
    - /url: /series/rfc/
  - paragraph:
    - text: RFCs outline computer networking and Internet foundations, including
    - link "Internet Standards":
      - /url: /search/?status=Internet+Standard
    - text: and historical or informative content. They are published by the RFC Editor for the
    - link "IETF (open in new window)":
      - /url: https://www.ietf.org
      - text: IETF
      - img "(open in new window)"
    - text: ","
    - link "IRTF (open in new window)":
      - /url: https://www.irtf.org
      - text: IRTF
      - img "(open in new window)"
    - text: ","
    - link "IAB (open in new window)":
      - /url: https://www.iab.org
      - text: IAB
      - img "(open in new window)"
    - text: ", and"
    - link "ISE (open in new window)":
      - /url: /authors/rfc-independent-submissions/
      - text: ISE
      - img "(open in new window)"
    - text: ", which collectively form the authoritative source for RFCs."
  - searchbox "Find an RFC (number, subseries, title, author, etc.)": "2616"
  - button "Submit search":
    - img
  - heading "Latest RFCs" [level=2]
  - paragraph:
    - text: Looking for works in progress? Go to
    - link "datatracker.ietf.org":
      - /url: https://datatracker.ietf.org
  - list:
    - listitem:
      - 'heading "RFC 10026: BCP 246: Operational Recommendations for DNSSEC Delegation Signer (DS) Automation" [level=3]':
        - link "RFC 10026:":
          - /url: /info/rfc10026/
        - link "BCP 246:":
          - /url: /info/bcp246/
        - text: Operational Recommendations for DNSSEC Delegation Signer (DS) Automation
      - text: Best Current Practice
      - list:
        - listitem: S. Sheng
        - listitem: P. Thomassen
      - list:
        - listitem: July 2026
        - listitem: IETF publication
        - listitem: Operations and Management Area
    - listitem:
      - 'heading "RFC 9997: YANG-CBOR: Allocating SID Ranges for Private Enterprise Number (PEN) Holders" [level=3]':
        - link "RFC 9997:":
          - /url: /info/rfc9997/
        - text: "YANG-CBOR: Allocating SID Ranges for Private Enterprise Number (PEN) Holders"
      - text: Proposed Standard
      - list:
        - listitem: C. Bormann
      - list:
        - listitem: July 2026
        - listitem: IETF publication
        - listitem: Web and Internet Transport
    - listitem:
      - 'heading "RFC 10004: Certificate Management over CMS (CMC): Compliance Requirements" [level=3]':
        - link "RFC 10004:":
          - /url: /info/rfc10004/
        - text: "Certificate Management over CMS (CMC): Compliance Requirements"
      - text: Proposed Standard
      - list:
        - listitem: J. Mandel, Ed.
        - listitem: S. Turner, Ed.
      - list:
        - listitem: July 2026
        - listitem: IETF publication
        - listitem: Security Area
  - heading "Learn about RFCs" [level=2]
  - list:
    - listitem:
      - heading "What Is an RFC?" [level=3]:
        - link "What Is an RFC?":
          - /url: /series/rfc/
      - paragraph: An introduction to RFCs and the organizations that produce them
    - listitem:
      - heading "Tips for Reading RFCs" [level=3]:
        - link "Tips for Reading RFCs":
          - /url: /series/rfc-tips/
      - paragraph: Helpful information about common conventions in RFCs
    - listitem:
      - heading "Errata in RFCs" [level=3]:
        - link "Errata in RFCs":
          - /url: /series/rfc-errata/
      - paragraph: Understand errors and corrections in RFCs
    - listitem:
      - heading "About the RFC Editor" [level=3]:
        - link "About the RFC Editor":
          - /url: /about/rfc-editor/
      - paragraph: RFC Editor publishes and archives official RFCs
  - heading "Browse RFCs" [level=2]
  - list:
    - listitem:
      - heading "Standards" [level=3]:
        - link "Standards":
          - /url: /search/?status=Internet+Standard
      - paragraph: Stable or mature protocols and services
    - listitem:
      - heading "Best Current Practices" [level=3]:
        - link "Best Current Practices":
          - /url: /search/?status=Best+Current+Practice
      - paragraph: Common guidelines for policies, operations, or procedures
    - listitem:
      - heading "Download RFCs" [level=3]:
        - link "Download RFCs":
          - /url: /series/rfc-download/
      - paragraph: Download, mirror or get a feed of RFCs
    - listitem:
      - heading "Browse all RFCs" [level=3]:
        - link "Browse all RFCs":
          - /url: /rfc-index/
  - heading "Start Participating" [level=2]
  - list:
    - listitem:
      - heading "Internet Engineering Task Force" [level=3]:
        - link "Internet Engineering Task Force":
          - /url: https://www.ietf.org
      - paragraph: Protocol standards, best current practices, experimental, and informational documents
    - listitem:
      - heading "Internet Research Task Force" [level=3]:
        - link "Internet Research Task Force":
          - /url: https://www.irtf.org
      - paragraph: Research issues related to the Internet
    - listitem:
      - heading "Internet Architecture Board" [level=3]:
        - link "Internet Architecture Board":
          - /url: https://www.iab.org
      - paragraph: Long-range technical direction for Internet development
    - listitem:
      - heading "Independent Submissions" [level=3]:
        - link "Independent Submissions":
          - /url: /authors/rfc-independent-submissions/
      - paragraph: How the Independent Submission Stream works.
